{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-12T19:51:48.479Z","data":{"text":"Done. The task's verify and the proposal's `pnpm verify` both pass.\n\n## Summary\n\n**`src/core/lifecycle/retry-plan-edits.ts`** (new) exports `assertPlanCommitted(projectRoot, specId, config)`:\n- Finds the change with `findChange`, returning without effect when it throws so `retrySpec` still reports a missing change itself.\n- Treats the change as in a worktree when `change.tree.worktreeFolder` is set; reads status through `selectVcs(change.tree.root, config)` and returns under `NoVcs`.\n- Checks both `path` and `from` of every status entry, as `worktreeDirt` does, and refuses any path inside the change folder other than its `tasks.md` and `.run/` with `Change <id> has plan edits not committed in its worktree: <paths>. Run osq approve <id> to approve them.`, paths relative to the change folder, sorted. Writes nothing.\n\n**`src/cli/retry.ts`**: `retryCommand` calls `assertPlanCommitted` inside its existing `try`, before `retrySpec` (which is unchanged), so the refusal reads `Error retrying <id> <target>:` then the message.\n\n**`tests/retry-plan-edits.test.ts`** (new): plain `node:test` cases proving every row of \"Plan edits not committed\" through `project.retry('1')` from `createRecoveryProject`, with a task dying `verify_red` at `autoRetries: 0`, writing each row's edits into `project.changeFolder` before the retry.\n\nBoth exported functions carry `@scenario watcher-and-harness: Plan edits not committed`."}}
